---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CinematicBackground from '../../components/CinematicBackground.astro';
import ExpandableContent from '../../components/ExpandableContent.astro';
---

<Layout title="The Paradigm Cosmos | EdLove">
    <CinematicBackground />

    <div class="relative z-10 pb-24 sanctuary-container">
        <!-- Header: The Mapping -->
        <section class="text-center space-y-12 mb-32 animate-fade-in-up">
            <div class="space-y-4">
                <span class="font-sans text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.4em] font-bold text-[var(--color-agedGold)] opacity-60">Domain I</span>
                <h1 class="text-7xl md:text-9xl font-serif text-[var(--color-midnightInk)] leading-none">The Paradigm Cosmos</h1>
            </div>

            <div class="h-px w-24 bg-[var(--color-agedGold)]/30 mx-auto"></div>

            <p class="font-serif text-2xl text-[var(--color-midnightInk)]/50 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed italic">
                "We map the constellations of how learning happens. <br/> From the factory floor to the forest floor."
            </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Narrative Flow: The Content -->
        <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-16">
            
            <ExpandableContent title="Biological Learning (Animal Wisdom)" subtitle="The Original Paradigm" icon="🐾">
                <div class="py-6 space-y-6 text-[var(--color-midnightInk)]/80">
                    <p class="text-2xl font-serif text-[var(--color-agedGold)] italic">"Humans are animals, too."</p>
                    <p>We forget this at our peril. For 99% of human history, "education" did not exist. Learning was simply <em>living</em>.</p>
                    <p>In this paradigm, learning is contextual, embodied, and social. Every other paradigm is an overlay on top of this fundamental truth.</p>
                </div>
            </ExpandableContent>

            <ExpandableContent title="Industrial Model (Modern Schooling)" subtitle="The Factory System" icon="🏭">
                <div class="py-6 space-y-6 text-[var(--color-midnightInk)]/80">
                    <p class="text-2xl font-serif text-[var(--color-agedGold)] italic">"The Factory of Compliance."</p>
                    <p>Born to serve the needs of industrialization. The goal was standardized workers who could follow instructions and tolerate boredom. This model is not broken—it is just obsolete.</p>
                </div>
            </ExpandableContent>

            <ExpandableContent title="Montessori" subtitle="Prepared Environment" icon="🧸">
                <div class="py-6 space-y-6 text-[var(--color-midnightInk)]/80">
                    <p class="text-2xl font-serif text-[var(--color-agedGold)] italic">"Follow the Child."</p>
                    <p>Maria Montessori discovered that children have an innate desire to learn. Here, the teacher is a gardener, preparing the soil and protecting the seed of concentration.</p>
                </div>
            </ExpandableContent>

            <ExpandableContent title="Democratic Education" subtitle="Radical Agency" icon="🗳️">
                <div class="py-6 space-y-6 text-[var(--color-midnightInk)]/80">
                    <p class="text-2xl font-serif text-[var(--color-agedGold)] italic">"No learning without consent."</p>
                    <p>Children are people with rights. You do not learn democracy by reading about it in a dictatorship; you learn it by practicing it.</p>
                </div>
            </ExpandableContent>

             <ExpandableContent title="Indigenous Knowledge Systems" subtitle="Land & Lineage" icon="🌿">
                <div class="py-6 space-y-6 text-[var(--color-midnightInk)]/80">
                    <p class="text-2xl font-serif text-[var(--color-agedGold)] italic">"We are the land."</p>
                    <p>Knowledge is not an object to be possessed; it is a relationship to be maintained. Integration of spirit and matter across generations.</p>
                </div>
            </ExpandableContent>

        </section>
    </div>
</Layout>
